                    // return() is called if it has one. This half's generator
                    // replays, so the body's `finally` has already run once per step
                    // (see the GENERATORS REPLAY note in the :description) and
                    // return() only marks it done - which is what makes a second loop
                    // over a partially consumed generator answer nothing, in BOTH
