                // structural test the for-of loops use - and one that is an array or a
                // string by index. Driving it lazily is what makes 'yield* endless()'
                // work: the doYield below throws out of the replay at the yield being
                // produced, so the delegate is only ever stepped as far as it is needed.
                // Before this a generator delegate answered no 'length' and contributed
                // NOTHING, which is what the compiler half's js_iterable drain hid.
